{
  "$comment": "vcpkg's boost-fiber with try-lock-owner-race.patch: try_lock read the owner after letting its spinlock go, a data race; remote-wake-notify.patch: a remote wake notified the scheduler after letting the queue's spinlock go, where the scheduler's thread could end and free it first; tsan-mutex-annotations.patch: the fibers' mutexes told to ThreadSanitizer as mutexes under BOOST_USE_TSAN, where it saw only their spinlocks' atomics. Drop each patch when Boost.Fiber fixes it upstream.",
  "name": "boost-fiber",
  "version": "1.92.0",
  "port-version": 3,
  "description": "Boost fiber module",
  "homepage": "https://www.boost.org/library/latest/fiber/",
  "documentation": "https://www.boost.org/libs/fiber",
  "license": "BSL-1.0",
  "supports": "!uwp & !(arm32 & windows) & !emscripten",
